","text":" block: a fuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(fires once, N turns after it is started) or a daemon (runs at the end of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every turn while active). The body is registered at bootstrap and never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serialized; only the schedule — name → turns remaining, or the active"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flag — lives in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WorldState"},{"type":"text","text":", so it saves and restores like any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state and a restore re-binds it to the declared body by name."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"}}}